  "summary": "The Iron Pagoda of Kaifeng, also called the Youguo Temple Pagoda, is an octagonal thirteen-storey brick tower built in 1049 under the Northern Song, after lightning burned an earlier tower in 1044. Brown glazed bricks give it an iron-like colour. China Daily and CGTN give its height as 55.08 metres.",
